    "wear": {
      "file": "shaft_sleeve_wear.glb",
      "title": "The sleeve wears, not the shaft",
      "description": "Packing (and some seal elastomers) rub on the shaft surface and slowly cut a groove, worst under the rings nearest the gland. A replaceable, hard-coated sleeve takes this wear and protects the expensive shaft from wear and corrosion; it is renewed at overhaul. The sleeve is keyed or clamped to turn with the shaft, located against the impeller hub, and sealed with an O-ring so liquid cannot creep along the shaft underneath. Check sleeve runout (≈ ≤ 0.05 mm TIR typical) after fitting.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
